# Ownership map · read by tools/ownership_check.py
#
# One rule per line:  <path-prefix>  <owner>
# Owners: any key from tracker/people.toml (upper-cased) | SHARED | GENERATED
#
#   <PERSON>    they own it. Nobody else changes it without a crossing note
#               (docs/00-RULES/OWNERSHIP-PROTOCOL.md).
#   SHARED      anyone may change it. Still reviewed.
#   GENERATED   nobody hand-edits it, ever. It is produced by a generator.
#
# Longest matching prefix wins, so a subdirectory can belong to someone else
# than its parent. Use that: it is how you make an ownership split visible in
# the directory tree, which is the only way it can be checked.
#
# Changing this file is itself a crossing: it needs both owners to approve.

# --- generated, never hand-edited -------------------------------------------
packages/shared                      GENERATED

# --- example: one service split by subpackage -------------------------------
services/api/handlers                ALEX
services/api                         ALEX
services/worker                      ALEX

apps/web                             SAM
apps/console                         SAM
infra                                SAM

# --- gates and infrastructure -----------------------------------------------
tools                                ALEX
.github                              ALEX
Makefile                             ALEX

# --- shared working areas ---------------------------------------------------
docs                                 SHARED
tracker                              SHARED
bench                                SHARED
spikes                               SHARED
fixtures                             SHARED
README.md                            SHARED

# --- files two sessions reliably conflict on: change alone, never in parallel
CLAUDE.md                            SHARED
docs/10-STATUS/NOW.md                SHARED
